//// A float held under a type parameter — a generic record's field, a
//// generic variant's payload — is the float on commonJS, erlang and beam.
//// wasm holds a float in a 4-byte slot as the address of its cell, and the
//// one body that reads `T` takes that address for the value: `300` printed
//// for `Box(value: 1.5).value` at exit 0 (`00 · gate-wasm-wrong-answers`).
//// Until a reader knows the cell, wasm refuses the value where it enters.

type Box<T>(value: T)

pub fn main() {
    val b = Box(value: 1.5);
    @print(b.value);
}
